7592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186260758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186261846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186260536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262570 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ffc75d90-c023-5fb9-a940-576505f511c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262960 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262960 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262960 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262960 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,5,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-4y+2z=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262960 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "875980ed-8584-5326-b58b-3349b4a511e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262960 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4y+2z & =2 \\\\ 4(1)-4(1)+2z & =2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-2,5,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-4,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+16+8|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312239 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312239 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312239 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23c37932-b8d1-516f-abf3-f1748834a7af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312486 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{48}{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312486 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312486 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f3b0406-2681-5fe8-a9d6-e948d2f27a69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312716 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{10\\sqrt{42}}{21}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312716 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312716 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5cdb367a-ee31-52bd-8e49-76ea1a5deb03" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312817 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{43}{11}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312817 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186312817 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6b7e35c1-be2d-55da-bd15-0ac93254cb95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313016 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313016 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313016 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "81295061-9129-54aa-abdf-5c3501c97825" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313242 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313242 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186313242 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a1272a18-c467-54d3-9f71-ae126c7eade1" 